Package: open-voice-input-linux
Version: @PACKAGE_VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Open Voice Input Linux contributors <SidUParis@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/SidUParis/openVoiceInput_linux
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), python3 (<< 3.13), python3-gi, desktop-file-utils, gir1.2-ibus-1.0, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, hicolor-icon-theme, ibus, ibus-gtk4, init-system-helpers (>= 1.65.2), libffi8, libportaudio2, libusb-1.0-0, pulseaudio-utils, systemd, xclip, wl-clipboard
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: native IBus voice input with inline preedit
 Open Voice Input Linux streams speech recognition into the focused IBus
 input context by default. It also offers an explicit remote-desktop mode that
 copies only the final text for manual paste. It includes a
 GTK settings application, adaptive terminology correction, dynamic
 microphone selection, and optional user-owned ASR data collection.
 .
 This Ubuntu 24.04 amd64 preview uses Volcengine ASR. Microphone audio is sent
 only after the user explicitly starts a dictation.
